A move adds budget to the destination and takes none from the source.
The processor would be promised more than once over;
the budgets of the shares add up to the whole processor.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: the budgets of the shares do not add up to the whole processor

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -342,7 +342,6 @@ void sched_share_move(struct share *from, struct share *to, uint32_t budget)
     if (moved > from->balance) {
         moved = from->balance;
     }
-    from->budget -= budget;
     from->balance -= moved;
     to->budget += budget;
     to->balance += moved;
